<section xml:id="section-differentiability" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>
    Differentiability
  </title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      The fundamental object in differential calculus is the <term> differentiable function </term> and its <term> derivative </term>. In this section, we formally differentiability as a property of real-valued functions defined on subsets of the real line <m> \R </m>. We will develop techniques of differentiation, compile a list of differentiable functions, and compare the regularities of various functions.
    </p>
  </introduction>

